# .env.example -- copy to .env and edit (install.sh does the copy for you).
#
# `.env` holds what is true of THIS MACHINE: where the binaries are, which
# ASR backend/model to load, and how to get out to the network. It is
# gitignored, which is why proxy credentials belong here and nowhere else.
#
# Every key is optional -- with ffmpeg and yt-dlp on PATH nothing needs
# configuring. Precedence: shell environment > .env > built-in default.
#
# NOTHING that changes a rendered pixel goes here. Style geometry, colour
# and type are constants in pipeline/render_default.py / render_bars.py,
# committed and reviewed -- a look-affecting value in an untracked file
# would make a render unreproducible from the repo alone.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binaries. Only needed when a tool is not on PATH, or to PIN an exact build.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#QC_FFMPEG=/opt/homebrew/bin/ffmpeg
#QC_FFPROBE=/opt/homebrew/bin/ffprobe
#QC_YT_DLP=/opt/homebrew/bin/yt-dlp


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Speech recognition (pipeline/transcribe.py).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# backend: mlx (Apple silicon) | faster (faster-whisper / CTranslate2, CPU or
# CUDA, portable). Default: mlx on Apple silicon, faster everywhere else.
#
# Switching backends RE-TIMES everything cut from a transcript: the two
# runtimes do not emit identical word boundaries. whisper.json records the
# backend that wrote it.
#QC_ASR_BACKEND=faster
#
# Model id OR an absolute path to a downloaded model directory -- both
# backends accept either, so an offline machine can point at local weights.
#QC_ASR_MODEL=mlx-community/whisper-large-v3-turbo
#QC_ASR_MODEL=/models/faster-whisper-large-v3-turbo-ct2
#
# Interpreter that can import the backend. Default: tools/asr-venv/bin/python
# (built by install.sh), falling back to the running python.
#QC_ASR_PYTHON=/path/to/asr-venv/bin/python


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Egress / proxy pool (pipeline/fetch.py --proxy). Needed on a cloud host,
# where YouTube bot-checks the datacentre IP outright. fetch.py is the ONLY
# script that leaves the machine; everything else is local.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Escalation is fixed: static residential -> datacentre -> fail. One sticky
# exit per fetch. Two measured constraints behind that order:
#  * A signed googlevideo URL embeds the exit IP that resolved it, so a
#    ROTATING proxy 403s the media fetch. Only sticky/static exits download.
#  * The bot check fires at the player-API stage, before any bytes move, and
#    burns PER EXIT IP. Moving to the next endpoint recovers; retrying one
#    endpoint harder makes it worse.
#
# Format: comma-separated user:pass@host:port (http:// is assumed).
#QC_PROXY_STATIC=user:pass@1.2.3.4:5001,user:pass@1.2.3.5:5002
#QC_PROXY_DATACENTER=user:pass@10.0.0.1:8001
